---
import Base from '../../../../layouts/Base.astro';

const SITE = 'https://precisionsolutionstech.com';
const title = 'Assay Privacy Policy | Precision Solutions Tech';
const description =
  'How Assay handles the files you open, convert and preview. Everything is processed on your Mac; the App Store version has no network access, no account and no analytics.';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${SITE}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Privacy Policy', item: `${SITE}/legal/privacy/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Assay', item: `${SITE}/legal/privacy/assay/` },
    ],
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'Assay Privacy Policy',
    url: `${SITE}/legal/privacy/assay/`,
    description,
    dateModified: '2026-09-25',
    isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', name: 'Precision Solutions Tech', url: `${SITE}/` },
  },
];
---

<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/legal/privacy/assay/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
        <li><a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a></li>
        <li>Assay</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <article class="prose">
      <h1>Assay Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="meta">Last updated: September 25, 2026</p>
      <p class="lead">
        This Privacy Policy describes how <strong>Assay</strong> (“we”, “us”) handles information when
        you use the Assay macOS application and its Finder and Quick Look extensions (the “App”),
        published by <strong>Precision Solutions Tech</strong>, operated by
        <strong>SG TECHNOLOGY LLC</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="summary">Short version</h2>
      <p>
        Assay runs <strong>on your Mac</strong>. The files you open, view, edit, convert and preview are
        processed locally and are never sent to us. The Mac App Store version of Assay has no network
        access at all. We operate no account system and no servers the App talks to, and we cannot see
        your files.
      </p>

      <h2 id="local">What the App processes locally</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Files you open</strong> — only files you choose: through the Open panel, by dropping
          them on the window or the Dock icon, with Open With, or from the Finder menu. macOS’s App
          Sandbox limits Assay to those files.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Files that belong with them</strong> — when you open a dBASE table or an SQLite
          database, Assay also reads the companion file macOS lets it read beside it (a memo
          <code>.fpt</code>/<code>.dbt</code> file, or a database’s <code>-wal</code> and
          <code>-shm</code> files), because the data you opened is partly stored there.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Conversions and edits</strong> — written only where you choose, in the Save panel or
          when you save a file in place. Some conversions use temporary copies in Assay’s own sandboxed
          temporary folder, which are deleted when the conversion finishes.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Quick Look previews</strong> — the Quick Look extension reads the one file Finder asks
          it to preview and produces the preview on your Mac. It has no network access and keeps
          nothing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The Finder menu</strong> — when you choose Open in Assay or Convert with Assay…, the
          extension records which file and which action in a container shared only by Assay and its
          extension, so the App knows what you asked for. The note is removed as soon as the App reads
          it, and expires after a minute if it is not.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Recent files and settings</strong> — a list of recently opened files (as macOS
          security bookmarks, so they can be reopened), the viewer you prefer for each kind of file, and
          whether the inspector is showing, stored in local preferences.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="network">Network access</h2>
      <p>
        The Mac App Store version of Assay does not have permission to use the network. It sends
        nothing and fetches nothing. Web pages, Markdown documents and emails are shown with anything
        they link to on the web left out: remote images are not loaded, which also stops tracking pixels
        in email from reporting that you opened a message.
      </p>

      <h2 id="purchases">Purchases</h2>
      <p>
        Assay is free to download. <strong>Assay Unlock</strong> is an in-app purchase made through the
        Mac App Store. Apple handles the payment under
        <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple’s Privacy Policy</a>. The App asks macOS
        whether your Apple ID owns the purchase; it does not see your Apple ID, your payment details or
        your identity, and we receive only the sales and payout reports Apple provides to developers,
        which do not identify you personally.
      </p>

      <h2 id="support">If you contact us</h2>
      <p>
        If you email support, we receive your email address and whatever you include in your message,
        and use them only to reply. Please do not send files that contain other people’s personal data
        unless it is needed to solve the problem.
      </p>

      <h2 id="analytics">Analytics, tracking, and advertising</h2>
      <p>
        The App contains <strong>no analytics SDKs, no advertising SDKs, and no third-party
        trackers</strong>. We do not profile you, and we do not sell or share personal information. If
        this ever changes, this policy will be updated before that change ships, and any collection
        would be opt-in.
      </p>

      <h2 id="files-you-hold">Other people’s information in your files</h2>
      <p>
        Files you open with Assay — spreadsheets, databases, email, contacts, calendars — may contain
        other people’s personal data. That data stays on your Mac and under your control; we never see
        it. You are responsible for handling it lawfully, including anything you convert or share.
      </p>

      <h2 id="retention">Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        Your files, conversions and edits remain wherever you saved them until you delete them.
        Temporary copies are deleted when the work that needed them finishes. Recent files and settings
        remain until you clear them (File → Open Recent → Clear Menu) or uninstall the App. Support
        emails are kept as long as needed to help you.
      </p>

      <h2 id="choices">Your rights and choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Open only the files you choose to; Assay cannot reach any others</li>
        <li>Turn the Finder and Quick Look extensions on or off in System Settings</li>
        <li>Clear the recent files list at any time</li>
        <li>Uninstall the App to remove it and its settings</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Because we do not collect your personal information, there is generally nothing for us to export
        or delete on request. If you have contacted support, you may ask us about the messages we hold.
      </p>

      <h2 id="children">Children’s privacy</h2>
      <p>The App is not directed to children under 13 (or the minimum age in your jurisdiction).</p>

      <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy. The “Last updated” date will change when we do. Continued use after
        an update means you accept the revised policy for subsequent use.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions:
        <a href="mailto:support@precisionsolutionstech.com">support@precisionsolutionstech.com</a>
        ·
        <a href="mailto:hello@precisionsolutionstech.com">hello@precisionsolutionstech.com</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/apps/assay/support/">Assay Support</a>
        · Company-wide policy:
        <a href="/legal/privacy/">Precision Solutions Tech Privacy Policy</a>
        · Company:
        <a href="/about/">About us</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
